                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "40926233-95c1-31f7-a743-e194f60c9110",
                        "entry_id": "f50e94fd-7ea9-3eac-98f6-1cd7f0e46d32",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что последовательный; неотступно следующий чему-либо, неуклонно проводящий в жизнь что-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d9e8181-0f1e-4fd7-a378-c2febc103418",
                                "sense_id": "40926233-95c1-31f7-a743-e194f60c9110",
                                "text": "Оба были очень бездарны, а поэтому очень прилежны и консеквентны до абсурда, но честны и благородны неизменно."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "556e3ef2-cfae-40a2-880c-6623b78406e7",
                                "sense_id": "40926233-95c1-31f7-a743-e194f60c9110",
                                "text": "Все же диалектика выше софистики, но обе до мозга костей неестественно сухи и, свою службу сослужив, сумели погубить древний мир, вредя и до современности, в которой выражены ярче всего у ярых законников и консеквентных метафизиков-мечтателей, полагающих, что к социальным явлениям можно прилагать приемы математики."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "070bfa3c-a7b8-3700-a2d1-af3610251384",
                        "entry_id": "f50e94fd-7ea9-3eac-98f6-1cd7f0e46d32",
                        "glosses": [
                            "геогр. следующий тем же путём, в том же направлении"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "56cb701f-8c0d-4428-8ff8-9eea5612a85b",
                        "source_entry_id": "f50e94fd-7ea9-3eac-98f6-1cd7f0e46d32",
                        "target_lang_word": "consequent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "consequent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2675f0e-16fb-3971-9de9-596df5340c16",
                                        "entry_id": "03463cc1-5b9e-3b99-95bc-230d0869a318",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Following as a result, inference, or natural effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa4dad13-db54-4baa-ac4a-540c1cdc199d",
                                                "sense_id": "e2675f0e-16fb-3971-9de9-596df5340c16",
                                                "text": "His retirement and consequent spare time enabled him to travel more."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "821b8e0e-2a12-40e6-8708-3b1272cc121c",
                                                "sense_id": "e2675f0e-16fb-3971-9de9-596df5340c16",
                                                "text": "The advantages are a saving in weight of about one ton, with consequent reduction in energy consumption; a saving in paint (of some three to four cwt. per car), with a corresponding economy on subsequent overhauls; and lower cleaning costs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04c06e95-762b-4df7-a6de-e4f545796ef3",
                                                "sense_id": "e2675f0e-16fb-3971-9de9-596df5340c16",
                                                "text": "Elsewhere in this issue, for example, an article on the new pattern of freight train operation in the N.E.R. consequent upon the opening this summer of its three mechanised marshalling yards shows that one effect will be a further step-up in the speed of the East Coast main line freight traffic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2133d2f-933f-3651-a14a-955e7605b853",
                                        "entry_id": "03463cc1-5b9e-3b99-95bc-230d0869a318",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to consequences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3166dc53-9854-3a38-8b9f-7a12bc8230cc",
                                        "entry_id": "03463cc1-5b9e-3b99-95bc-230d0869a318",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a stream, having a course determined by the slope it formed on."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "consequent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca3ebaad-18e1-3fce-a876-12197e979c16",
                                        "entry_id": "789250c9-ac7c-3c39-8d60-d6ca76e9ad6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The second half of a hypothetical proposition; Q, if the form of the proposition is \\\"If P, then Q.\\"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa8e5784-a23e-3244-881e-206c445d750f",
                                        "entry_id": "789250c9-ac7c-3c39-8d60-d6ca76e9ad6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An event which follows another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e26317c9-f256-4376-a502-38fcf3f96c87",
                                                "sense_id": "aa8e5784-a23e-3244-881e-206c445d750f",
                                                "text": "They were ill-governed, which is always a consequent of ill payment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2e4646e-1712-325f-bbba-8a438712947d",
                                        "entry_id": "789250c9-ac7c-3c39-8d60-d6ca76e9ad6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The second term of a ratio, i.e. the term b in the ratio a:b, the other being the antecedent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2df9c76d-2ac6-3f26-95f1-658b4e121513",
                                        "entry_id": "789250c9-ac7c-3c39-8d60-d6ca76e9ad6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A consequent stream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19cd3efd-006b-4b49-b114-4683431a6f98",
                                                "sense_id": "2df9c76d-2ac6-3f26-95f1-658b4e121513",
                                                "text": "Consequents cannot get any better off than at first: they get all the drainage and cannot get more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
